1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,504
How do you install the same system on a laptop and inside a bank?

2
00:00:03,554 --> 00:00:08,544
Picture a product installed once, by hand, by someone who has since moved on.

3
00:00:08,594 --> 00:00:14,640
Months later, nobody knows which values production runs with, or why the test server behaves differently.

4
00:00:14,690 --> 00:00:18,912
An install nobody can repeat is an install nobody understands.

5
00:00:18,962 --> 00:00:20,928
Think of the cook from Lesson 6.

6
00:00:20,978 --> 00:00:24,096
The cook follows one recipe in every kitchen.

7
00:00:24,146 --> 00:00:26,616
Only where the ingredients come from changes.

8
00:00:26,666 --> 00:00:28,488
Our install works the same way.

9
00:00:28,538 --> 00:00:32,520
The steps are identical on a laptop, a test server and production.

10
00:00:32,570 --> 00:00:37,128
Only the values differ, and each environment's values are written down once.

11
00:00:37,178 --> 00:00:44,448
A value is anything that belongs to this bank in this place: an address, a certificate, an email for alerts.

12
00:00:44,498 --> 00:00:48,384
The card zone has its own values, and the bank sets every one.

13
00:00:48,434 --> 00:00:52,248
Who may call the card zone, and which roles each caller may use.

14
00:00:52,298 --> 00:01:00,888
The fraud limits from Lesson 14: how many refused tries a card, its first digits, an address or a shop may have within a window of time.

15
00:01:00,938 --> 00:01:06,552
How long a card-entry session lives, how many tries it allows, and how long a code lives.

16
00:01:06,602 --> 00:01:08,616
Each is the bank's chosen value.

17
00:01:08,666 --> 00:01:11,328
Nothing has a default, and nothing is guessed.

18
00:01:11,378 --> 00:01:15,360
The bank sets them once for each environment, and they are kept in Vault.

19
00:01:15,410 --> 00:01:17,232
Order matters too.

20
00:01:17,282 --> 00:01:19,632
The card zone installs first.

21
00:01:19,682 --> 00:01:25,416
ecom then asks the card zone for its certificate, waits until it is signed, and carries on.

22
00:01:25,466 --> 00:01:28,680
Before anything is installed, a preflight runs.

23
00:01:28,730 --> 00:01:32,136
A preflight is a check of the machine before any work starts.

24
00:01:32,186 --> 00:01:36,216
It looks for what the install needs, such as the right tools and free ports.

25
00:01:36,266 --> 00:01:39,864
When something is missing, it says exactly what to fix.

26
00:01:39,914 --> 00:01:44,136
Then Vault is set up, and every service's settings are written from it.

27
00:01:44,186 --> 00:01:47,952
The services start in order, each one waiting for what it needs.

28
00:01:48,002 --> 00:01:54,600
A later change is just a new value, applied the same way, and only the services that use it restart.

29
00:01:54,650 --> 00:02:01,752
Every install ends with a health check: each service is asked whether it is ready, and answers a clear yes or no.

30
00:02:01,802 --> 00:02:03,624
Let's watch the product.

31
00:02:03,674 --> 00:02:07,488
An operator starts the card zone's installer on a fresh server.

32
00:02:07,538 --> 00:02:09,576
The preflight runs first.

33
00:02:09,626 --> 00:02:11,448
Most lines pass.

34
00:02:11,498 --> 00:02:14,832
One line fails, and right under it is the fix.

35
00:02:14,882 --> 00:02:17,208
The operator fixes it and starts again.

36
00:02:17,258 --> 00:02:19,080
Now everything passes.

37
00:02:19,130 --> 00:02:21,480
The installer asks for the release to run.

38
00:02:21,530 --> 00:02:24,144
Then it asks for the bank's values, one at a time.

39
00:02:24,194 --> 00:02:26,016
Where each door listens.

40
00:02:26,066 --> 00:02:28,080
Which callers may use the card zone.

41
00:02:28,130 --> 00:02:34,824
For each caller, the websites it serves, how long a card-entry session lives, and how many tries it allows.

42
00:02:34,874 --> 00:02:39,792
Then the fraud limits, the addresses for alerts, and the certificate for the payers' door.

43
00:02:39,842 --> 00:02:42,264
Every answer is checked as it is given.

44
00:02:42,314 --> 00:02:44,784
An answer in the wrong form is asked again.

45
00:02:44,834 --> 00:02:49,416
A certificate that does not match its key is asked again, with the reason.

46
00:02:49,466 --> 00:02:54,216
When every value is there, the installer says so, and how many it asked.

47
00:02:54,266 --> 00:02:59,616
It starts the services in order, and ends with the health check: every service healthy.

48
00:02:59,666 --> 00:03:02,472
Then the operator runs ecom's installer.

49
00:03:02,522 --> 00:03:07,056
It asks for its own values, sends its certificate request, and waits.

50
00:03:07,106 --> 00:03:09,744
On the card zone, the request is signed.

51
00:03:09,794 --> 00:03:14,304
ecom carries on, and its own health check shows every service healthy too.

52
00:03:14,354 --> 00:03:16,176
What does this protect?

53
00:03:16,226 --> 00:03:23,184
It protects the bank from an install nobody can explain: every value is written down, once, in one place.

54
00:03:23,234 --> 00:03:28,992
It protects production from a guess: a missing value stops the install instead of being filled in.

55
00:03:29,042 --> 00:03:34,056
And it protects testing: what works on a laptop is the same install that runs in the bank.

56
00:03:34,106 --> 00:03:35,928
Back to the kitchens.

57
00:03:35,978 --> 00:03:40,680
One recipe, three kitchens, and only the ingredients change.

58
00:03:40,730 --> 00:03:43,752
Next: how a release is numbered and shipped.
